// The canonical `tgc` value, host side, and its two encodings.
//
// `TVal` mirrors the frozen rec group in `tgc/abi` arm for arm: this is what a
// host holds when it is looking at a value it did not build, and what the codecs
// read and write. It is deliberately NOT `core.Value` yet — phase 4 folds the
// two together rather than keeping a mirror forever, and until then a mirror is
// what lets the format be checked without moving the framework under it.
//
// Two encodings, two jobs. CBOR is FAITHFUL: every arm survives, and one that
// cannot be encoded is an error rather than a silent null. JSON is
// INTERCHANGE: it is what an agent writes by hand and what a browser parses, so
// it is `$`-tagged and it loses the Int/Num distinction on the way back in. Both
// facts are stated rather than hidden.
import {
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/tgc/abi",
  "moonbitlang/x/codec/base64",
  "moonbitlang/x/encoding",
  "moonbitlang/x/time",
  "moonbitlang/core/debug",
  "moonbitlang/core/json",
  "moonbitlang/core/set",
  "moonbitlang/core/string",
}
